  "definition": "A satellite link budget is an auditable calculation of the gains, losses and noise between a transmitter and receiver. It tests whether a chosen waveform and data rate meet their required carrier quality with adequate margin for a stated geometry and operating case. Separate budgets are normally needed for uplink and downlink, and for combinations of ground station, spacecraft antenna, data rate and mission phase.[^1]",
